      "hints": [
        "Use the binomial formula $\\binom{6}{r}2^{6-r}(-\\frac{1}{2}x)^r$ for $r = 0, 1, 2, 3$.",
        "Evaluate each term carefully."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write the binomial expansion of $\\left(2 - \\frac{1}{2}x\\right)^6$ up to the term in $x^3$:\n$$\\left(2 - \\frac{1}{2}x\\right)^6 = \\binom{6}{0}2^6 + \\binom{6}{1}2^5\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}x\\right) + \\binom{6}{2}2^4\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}x\\right)^2 + \\binom{6}{3}2^3\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}x\\right)^3 + \\dots$$",
        "Evaluate the individual terms:\n$$\\binom{6}{0}2^6 = 1 \\times 64 = 64$$\n$$\\binom{6}{1}2^5\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}x\\right) = 6 \\times 32 \\times \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}x\\right) = -96x$$\n$$\\binom{6}{2}2^4\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}x\\right)^2 = 15 \\times 16 \\times \\frac{1}{4}x^2 = 60x^2$$\n$$\\binom{6}{3}2^3\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}x\\right)^3 = 20 \\times 8 \\times \\left(-\\frac{1}{8}x^3\\right) = -20x^3$$",
        "Combine the terms:\n$$\\left(2 - \\frac{1}{2}x\\right)^6 = 64 - 96x + 60x^2 - 20x^3 + \\dots$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Binomial Expansion": "Applies binomial formula (M1) and simplifies to $64 - 96x + 60x^2 - 20x^3$ (A2)."
        },
